From a93db9ad9f3fd1dd870c267e2c6fda942caa1e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:39:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: spm: fix the SDM660 silver L2 AVS control value

The power cluster L2 SAW of SDM660 is programmed with an AVS control
value that differs from the one the vendor kernel uses for this SAW
(0x1010031), so the AVS hardware runs with the wrong configuration.

Use the vendor value.

Fixes: 13e72c3e2261 ("soc: qcom: spm: Implement support for SAWv4.1, SDM630/660 L2 AVS")
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261019-fix-qcom-saw-v1-1-9c7ba3fc2493@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <andersson@kernel.org>

Backport this prerequisite to maintained Linux 6.18.63. The complete
seventeen-change batch passes native ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT object
builds with the MSM8926 feature enabled and disabled. CPU-idle is ARM
only. Host fault models use synthetic services and normal LeakSanitizer;
firmware, electrical and physical suspend acceptance remain open.

Codex prepared this local backport and verification. Original authors,
dates, licenses and human attribution tags are retained. Human DCO and
review remain pending. No phone access or publication occurred.

Backported from commit 8b5c5b0e431a ("soc: qcom: spm: fix the SDM660
silver L2 AVS control value")
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c
index ebd32ad69ce12..b983a27f7f0c5 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c
@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ static const struct spm_reg_data spm_reg_660_gold_l2  = {
 
 static const struct spm_reg_data spm_reg_660_silver_l2  = {
 	.reg_offset = spm_reg_offset_v4_1,
-	.avs_ctl = 0x101c031,
+	.avs_ctl = 0x1010031,
 	.avs_limit = 0x4580458,
 };
 
-- 
2.56.0

